    <paragraph>Graph Quadratic Functions of the form $$f(x) = \left( {x - h} \right)^{2}$$</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, ⓐ graph the quadratic functions on the same rectangular coordinate system and ⓑ describe what effect adding a constant, $$h$$ , inside the parentheses has</paragraph>
    <exercise number="301" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = x^{2}, g(x) = \left( {x - 3} \right)^{2},$$ and $$h(x) = \left( {x + 3} \right)^{2}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓑ The graph of $$g(x)=(x-3)2g(x)=(x-3)2$$ is the same as the graph of $$f(x)=x2f(x)=x2$$ but shifted right 3 units. The graph of $$h(x)=(x+3)2h(x)=(x+3)2$$ is the same as the graph of $$f(x)=x2f(x)=x2$$ but shifted left 3 units.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
